Streaming sub-agents
python
When a create_agent call invokes another named create_agent (via a wrapping tool,
typically), the inner agent's events flow at a nested namespace. The name= you pass to
create_agent identifies that inner agent in the stream, so you can filter and label per agent.
Named sub-agents surface on the dedicated stream.subagents projection. Each handle
exposes the inner agent's own .messages , .values , .tool_calls , and .output , plus .name
(the name= you passed) and .cause (the tool call that dispatched the sub-agent). Because
only named create_agent runs appear here, you don't need to filter plain subgraphs out.
