Each stage processes events independently and concurrently: audio transcription begins as
soon as audio arrives, the agent starts reasoning as soon as a transcript is available, and
speech synthesis begins as soon as agent text is generated. This architecture can achieve
sub-700ms latency to support natural conversation.
