Middleware-registered transformers require langchain@1.4.3 or later.
Middleware can register stream transformer factories that project events from the live
agent stream onto typed extension channels. This is useful for surfacing counters, side-
channel artifacts, partial outputs, or wire-level redaction without coupling to the
framework's built-in projections.
At compile time, middleware-registered factories merge with anything the caller passes
directly to the agent factory. The final ordering rules keep the built-in ToolCallTransformer
in front and let caller-supplied entries land last.
