Summary
Choose the Graph API when you need explicit control over workflow structure, complex branching,
parallel processing, or team collaboration benefits.
Choose the Functional API when you want to add LangGraph features to existing code with
minimal changes, have simple linear workflows, or need rapid prototyping capabilities.
Both APIs provide the same core LangGraph features (persistence, streaming, human-in-the-loop,
memory) but package them in different paradigms to suit different development styles and use
cases.

