Execution
Tasks can only be called from within an entrypoint, another task, or a state graph node.
Tasks cannot be called directly from the main application code.
python
When you call a task, it returns immediately with a future object. A future is a placeholder for a
result that will be available later.
To obtain the result of a task, you can either wait for it synchronously (using result() ) or await
it asynchronously (using await ).
