By default, the graph will have the same input and output schemas. If you want to change this,
you can also specify explicit input and output schemas directly. This is useful when you have a
lot of keys, and some are explicitly for input and others for output.
Multiple schemas
Typically, all graph nodes communicate with a single schema. This means that they will read and
write to the same state channels. But, there are cases where we want more control over this:
Internal nodes can pass information that is not required in the graph's input / output.

