Working with messages in graph state
Why use messages?
Most modern LLM providers have a chat model interface that accepts a list of messages as input.
LangChain's chat model interface in particular accepts a list of message objects as inputs. These
messages come in a variety of forms such as @[ HumanMessage ] (user input) or @[ AIMessage ] (LLM
response).
To read more about what message objects are, please refer to the Messages conceptual guide.
