Re-execution and idempotency
python
When you compile with a checkpointer, LangGraph saves checkpoints at super-step
boundaries, not mid-function inside a node. If execution stops and later resumes (for example
after an interrupt or a retry), the affected node runs again from the start of its function. Code
and side effects before the pause run again.
