Do not wrap interrupt calls in try/catch
The way that @[ interrupt ] pauses execution at the point of the call is by throwing a special
exception. If you wrap the @[ interrupt ] call in a try/catch block, you will catch this exception
and the interrupt will not be passed back to the graph.
✅ Separate @[ interrupt ] calls from error-prone code
✅ Conditionally catch errors if needed
