Do not reorder interrupt calls within a node
It's common to use multiple interrupts in a single node, however this can lead to unexpected
behavior if not handled carefully.
When a node contains multiple interrupt calls, LangGraph keeps a list of resume values specific to
the task executing the node. Whenever execution resumes, it starts at the beginning of the node.
For each interrupt encountered, LangGraph checks if a matching value exists in the task's resume

