Combine control flow and state updates with Command
It can be useful to combine control flow (edges) and state updates (nodes). For example, you might
want to BOTH perform state updates AND decide which node to go to next in the SAME node.
LangGraph provides a way to do so by returning a @[Command] object from node functions:
