Layer 3: Execute. The model calls the tool with full knowledge of its interface, having loaded only
the definitions it needed.
This pattern reduces token usage dramatically and can improve tool selection accuracy: the model
focuses on a few relevant tools rather than scanning hundreds of irrelevant ones. Other discovery
strategies (embeddings, subagents, etc.) follow the same layered principle but substitute different
retrieval mechanisms in the catalog layer.
