Receiving Notifications
All notifications delivered on the stream carry io.modelcontextprotocol/subscriptionId in _meta ,
identifying the subscriptions/listen request that opened the stream. The value is the JSON-RPC ID
of the subscriptions/listen request. In the examples above, the request used "id": 1 , so the
acknowledgment and all subsequent notifications carry the subscription ID 1 . On stdio, where all
messages share a single channel, clients MUST use this field to correlate notifications with their
originating subscription.
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "method": "notifications/resources/updated",
  "params": {
    "_meta": {
      "io.modelcontextprotocol/subscriptionId": 1
